14:16.819 --> 14:18.709
- Will you marry me?
- Oh, Brian.

14:18.952 --> 14:19.953
Yes.

14:20.137 --> 14:22.477
Yes, Brian, I'll marry you!

14:24.673 --> 14:27.032
Hey, Mom. Hey, Brian.
We'll be upstairs.

14:27.115 --> 14:28.830
Yo, Rita, you want in on this?

14:28.914 --> 14:31.334
No, thanks.
We just got engaged!

14:31.418 --> 14:33.035
I'm faithful to Brian now.

14:33.118 --> 14:35.495
Whatever.
This ain't even my whole night.

14:39.862 --> 14:41.120
You're engaged?!

14:41.203 --> 14:43.694
Yes. Rita and I are getting married.

14:43.777 --> 14:46.358
My God,
I can't even react big enough.

14:46.441 --> 14:47.602
Here's Mrs. Garrett.

14:47.685 --> 14:48.845
What?!

14:49.333 --> 14:52.197
Look, if my happiness means
so little to you all that you have

14:52.281 --> 14:55.667
Charlotte Rae just standing by to crack
a joke, then you really disappoint me.

14:55.751 --> 14:58.094
Look, Brian,
I apologize for the other night.

14:58.177 --> 15:00.383
We... we were all very insensitive.

15:00.671 --> 15:04.506
And if this is what you want,
we as a family, support your decision.

15:04.590 --> 15:06.862
I don't.
I'd... I'd rather you marry

15:06.945 --> 15:11.572
a... a... a... a... a... a... a...
a Japanese or something.

15:11.740 --> 15:13.046
I'm with you, too, buddy.

15:13.130 --> 15:16.382
In twenty years, she'll be seventy,
and you'll have been dead for fifteen years.

15:16.465 --> 15:17.847
God bless the both of yous.

15:22.031 --> 15:23.551
Hey, it's 4:30.

15:23.634 --> 15:26.200
Isn't there an early bird special
you should be running off to?

15:26.283 --> 15:28.370
She's fifty, Stewie.
She's not an old woman.

15:29.554 --> 15:31.303
Hello?
Hey, Rita.

15:32.624 --> 15:34.447
Uh, no, I'm not hungry yet.

15:36.117 --> 15:38.947
Well, if we get there by 5:30,
I'm sure they'll honor it.

15:39.030 --> 15:41.063
Brian, is she calling
dinner "supper?"

15:41.146 --> 15:43.061
So, what are you doing
this afternoon?

15:43.144 --> 15:46.033
"Oh, I'm just sorting out my
pills for the week, sweetie. "

15:46.116 --> 15:48.275
Well, you do that,
and I'll be over a little later.

15:48.358 --> 15:49.693
Huh? Did I get it?

15:49.776 --> 15:52.016
Was she sorting out
her pills for the week?

15:52.099 --> 15:55.151
In that little plastic thing
with the seven boxes? Hmm?

15:55.234 --> 15:58.256
Actually, she just got back from the gym,
and she's jumping in the shower.

15:58.666 --> 16:01.134
- She got a chair in that shower?
- Shut up!

16:01.427 --> 16:05.480
Have archaeologists ever discovered
Ancient Egyptian pottery in her vagina?

16:05.563 --> 16:08.157
You know what? That one was too wordy.
That one was too wordy.

16:08.239 --> 16:10.302
That... that was...
that was flawed from the ground up.

16:10.385 --> 16:12.432
It wasn't funny,
and we'll work on it

16:12.969 --> 16:14.238
and get back to you.

16:18.490 --> 16:19.751
- Hey, Rita?
- Yeah?

16:19.834 --> 16:23.005
- Where do you keep your toothpaste?
- What are you looking for, tooth polish?

16:23.088 --> 16:25.615
- Toothpaste, yeah.
- Just use the baking soda.

16:25.699 --> 16:26.792
"Baking soda"?

16:26.875 --> 16:28.534
Ah, what the hell,
I can skip a night.

16:28.778 --> 16:32.087
Oh, I've never noticed this picture before.
Is that you when you were a little girl?

16:32.255 --> 16:35.054
Oh, yeah. That's the summer
my family went to DC.

16:35.223 --> 16:38.567
That, uh, flag's missing
some stars there.

16:38.735 --> 16:40.513
Why don't you come to bed, Brian?

16:40.596 --> 16:43.018
What do you say we make
a little whoopee?

16:43.101 --> 16:44.533
Yeah, sure. Why not?

16:48.706 --> 16:50.769
You're okay?
I'm not hurting you, am I?

16:50.852 --> 16:52.919
No, I'm fine.
What are you talking about?

16:53.002 --> 16:54.876
I just want to make sure
you're comfortable.

16:57.198 --> 16:58.619
Oh, I love you, Brian!

16:58.837 --> 17:00.078
Sock it to me!

17:00.161 --> 17:01.225
- What?!
- Ouch!

17:01.308 --> 17:03.039
- What's wrong?!
- Oh, nothing.

17:03.122 --> 17:06.572
When I'm on my back, sometimes
my breast can slide in my armpit.

17:06.655 --> 17:08.509
Just got pinched, that's all.

17:08.593 --> 17:09.595
Okay.

17:14.034 --> 17:15.839
- Was that your boob?
- God, no!

17:16.236 --> 17:17.635
I think I broke my hip!

17:17.785 --> 17:19.372
Oh, my God!
Wh... wh... wh... what should I do?

17:19.384 --> 17:21.232
Call the number on my bracelet!

17:21.587 --> 17:23.968
It says, "Murray Hill, 4185."

17:24.051 --> 17:26.517
- that's not enough numbers!
- That's the number, Brian!

17:26.600 --> 17:28.791
Just dial zero and read it to Sarah.

17:28.874 --> 17:30.111
For God's sake, Rita!

17:33.435 --> 17:34.437
She's fine.

17:34.521 --> 17:36.215
She's out of surgery and she's resting.

17:36.384 --> 17:38.626
Well, how did she break it?
Did she fall?

17:38.709 --> 17:41.482
Well, uh... She...
Yes, she fell.

17:41.650 --> 17:44.525
Boy, you know, Brian, a woman her age
comes in here, they don't always leave.

17:44.609 --> 17:46.025
Peter, she's going to be okay.

17:46.108 --> 17:47.591
Listen, Brian, you say the word

17:47.674 --> 17:50.373
and I'll go in there with a pillow
and you won't have any more problems.

17:50.456 --> 17:53.231
How many times do I have to tell you,
I'm sticking by this woman?

17:53.314 --> 17:54.965
- I love her.
- Careful, Brian.

17:55.049 --> 17:57.210
Sometimes the things you
love can disappoint you.

17:57.293 --> 17:58.671
<i>Like that Playboy issue.</i>

17:58.999 --> 18:00.060
Ah, here we go.

18:00.143 --> 18:02.251
<i>Playboy's "Women of the Olympics."</i>

18:02.576 --> 18:04.431
Wow, those are some broad shoulders.

18:05.064 --> 18:07.402
Okay, I guess small boobs
are good for swimming.

18:08.341 --> 18:10.878
That... that... those are balls.

18:15.425 --> 18:17.943
Brian?!
Brian?!

18:18.984 --> 18:20.778
Oh. Is the soup ready?

18:20.946 --> 18:23.849
- Yeah, got it right here.
- Oh, good. I need to take my pills.

18:23.932 --> 18:25.258
It's been three hours.

18:25.801 --> 18:29.555
You know, they warned me these blue ones
were going to make me constipated.

18:29.638 --> 18:31.329
- Right they were.
- Okay.

18:31.412 --> 18:33.238
I am plugged up.

18:33.321 --> 18:34.855
No, I... I got it.

18:38.062 --> 18:40.334
Do it, Brian.
Do it.

18:41.794 --> 18:43.069
It's me as a pillow.

18:43.478 --> 18:44.745
You know what, Brian?

18:44.828 --> 18:47.170
Oh, I could really use
some milk of magnesia.

18:47.253 --> 18:49.239
Okay, well, I'll go pick some up.

18:49.323 --> 18:51.057
Thanks, Brian.
I love you.

18:51.360 --> 18:54.494
Oh, and... and if you're going out,
get some milk of magnesia.

18:54.577 --> 18:55.895
Yeah, you just said that.

19:06.027 --> 19:08.351
<i>I am plugged up.</i>

19:14.947 --> 19:17.036
Wow, you are really pretty.

19:17.287 --> 19:18.290
Thanks.

19:18.609 --> 19:21.023
You know, uh, I wrote a book.

19:21.297 --> 19:22.416
What's that?

19:22.499 --> 19:23.918
It's like a long magazine.

19:24.001 --> 19:26.405
Huh? It's like the Internet
made out of a tree.

19:26.702 --> 19:29.968
Oh. Weird. You want to have
sex in the bathroom?

19:30.051 --> 19:33.958
Oh, gosh, what a treat.
Yes. Yes, I... I would... I would like that.

19:38.902 --> 19:41.058
Boy, that took you a long time.

19:41.141 --> 19:43.006
Did you have to wait
for the streetcar?

19:43.089 --> 19:45.388
Look, Rita,
I have a confession to make.

19:45.556 --> 19:47.659
I met a girl,
I had a couple of drinks,

19:47.742 --> 19:49.862
- and I slept with her.
- You what?

19:50.030 --> 19:52.827
I know, I feel awful.
It was a terrible thing to do.

19:52.910 --> 19:55.191
I'm so sorry.
It'll never happen again.

19:55.275 --> 19:56.860
But there's an upside.

19:56.943 --> 20:01.154
You see, these past few weeks I've been
doubting whether we're compatible,

20:01.238 --> 20:05.709
you know, because of the age difference.
But I realized that that doesn't matter.

20:05.792 --> 20:08.890
That what... what I get from you
is what I always wanted:

20:08.973 --> 20:11.361
a smart, sexy, real person

20:11.444 --> 20:14.541
who I can talk with and share
every piece of me with.

20:15.086 --> 20:18.042
I had a moment of weakness today,
but in a way, it's all right

20:18.125 --> 20:22.086
because it's taken me to a place where
I now realize that you're not too old for me.

20:22.169 --> 20:23.387
Isn't that great?

20:23.470 --> 20:25.098
You're not too old for me!

20:25.438 --> 20:26.863
You know what, Brian?

20:26.946 --> 20:28.434
You're not old enough for me.

20:28.517 --> 20:30.273
- What?
- You cheated on me.

20:30.356 --> 20:32.040
That's what happened today.

20:32.123 --> 20:35.016
You can rationalize it any
way you want, but to me,

20:35.099 --> 20:37.355
all that shows is that
you're an immature guy

20:37.437 --> 20:39.405
who doesn't realize
what a catch I am.

20:39.488 --> 20:42.066
I'm sorry, Brian,
but you screwed up.

20:42.149 --> 20:43.669
Now, please go.

20:43.752 --> 20:45.205
- But, Rita...
- Go!

20:45.505 --> 20:48.295
You can leave my apartment
key on the davenport.

20:49.561 --> 20:50.562
Here?

20:50.730 --> 20:52.901
No, the davenport...
The chesterfield.

20:54.242 --> 20:55.244
On this?

20:55.412 --> 20:57.460
No, does that look
like a divan to you?

20:58.423 --> 20:59.424
Here?

20:59.592 --> 21:01.772
Ugh. Leave them on the chifforobe.

21:01.856 --> 21:03.617
You know what? Just take your (bleep) keys.

21:03.700 --> 21:05.769
I don't know what
the (bleep) you're talking about.

21:05.770 --> 22:06.770
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru